{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778979115537,"sessionID":"ses_1cc98af08ffe44aQQ6lSUY8OpG","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_DEhd9qmUJIh4ZJsy2dMzZMi8","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+Implemented in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+Added new grouping term `MONDO:7770018` `podocytopathy` under `MONDO:0019722` and classified `minimal change disease` and `focal segmental glomerulosclerosis` under it, based on the cited literature.\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+Added a new MONDO grouping term for `podocytopathy` and placed the two issue-listed example children beneath it.\n+\n+Changes made:\n+- Added `MONDO:7770018` `podocytopathy` as a `disease_grouping` term under `MONDO:0019722` `glomerular disorder`.\n+- Added a text definition based on the issue-provided description and supported it with `PMID:25684864`, `PMID:32792490`, and `PMID:38804512`.\n+- Added issue tracking metadata pointing to `https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/10149`.\n+- Added the requester ORCID as creator metadata on the new term.\n+- Added `is_a: MONDO:7770018 ! podocytopathy` to:\n+  - `MONDO:0006835` `minimal change disease`\n+  - `MONDO:0100313` `focal segmental glomerulosclerosis`\n+\n+Rationale:\n+- The issue requested a new grouping term for podocyte-driven glomerular diseases.\n+- The cited literature supports podocytopathy as a glomerular disease grouping centered on structural or functional podocyte impairment leading to proteinuria or nephrotic syndrome.\n+- `minimal change disease` and `focal segmental glomerulosclerosis` are explicitly discussed in the cited literature as characteristic podocytopathy manifestations, so they were added as children without removing any existing parents.\n+\n+Validation completed:\n+- Read the imported issue context from `__issue_context__.json`.\n+- Verified the cited PMIDs exist and are contextually appropriate using PubMed web pages:\n+  - `PMID:32792490` `Podocytopathies`\n+  - `PMID:25684864` `Understanding podocytopathy and its relevance to clinical nephrology`\n+  - `PMID:38804512` `Autoantibodies Targeting Nephrin in Podocytopathies`\n+- Confirmed there was no pre-existing `podocytopathy` term in `mondo-edit.obo`.\n+- Confirmed the requested parent `MONDO:0019722` and child terms already exist.\n+- Ran a syntax check successfully with:\n+  - `robot convert --catalog src/ontology/catalog-v001.xml -i src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo -f obo -o src/ontology/mondo-edit.TMP.obo`\n+\n+Validation limitation:\n+- Repo guidance recommends normalization via ODK/docker (`make NORM` through `src/ontology/run.sh` or equivalent), but `docker` is not available in this environment, so I could not run the normalization step here.\n+\n+Checklist:\n+- [x] Read issue context\n+- [x] Verified cited publications\n+- [x] Confirmed parent and child terms exist\n+- [x] Added new `MONDO:777xxxx` term with metadata\n+- [x] Reparented requested child terms by adding new `is_a` axioms only\n+- [x] Checked in edits to `src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo`\n+- [x] Ran direct `robot convert` syntax validation\n+- [x] Committed only the ontology file change\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\nA PR_COMMENTS.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@\n+Implemented in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+Added new grouping term `MONDO:7770018` `podocytopathy` under `MONDO:0019722` and classified `minimal change disease` and `focal segmental glomerulosclerosis` under it, based on the cited literature.\n\nIndex: /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/PR_COMMENTS.md\n=